[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5329510016","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122544#issuecomment-5329510016","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122544","id":5329510016,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPanegA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T14:20:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T14:20:31Z","body":"> My Interpretation\r\n>\r\n> There is a minor regression.\r\n\r\nIs this something you plan to solve? Should this be a draft PR? This causing a regression sounds like a clear reason not to merge until that is fixed","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5329510016/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5330519090","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122544#issuecomment-5330519090","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122544","id":5330519090,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPblEMg","user":{"login":"Brogolem35","id":29329606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzI5NjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29329606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35","html_url":"https://github.com/Brogolem35","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T15:38:55Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T15:38:55Z","body":"> > My Interpretation\r\n> > There is a minor regression.\r\n> \r\n> Is this something you plan to solve? Should this be a draft PR? This causing a regression sounds like a clear reason not to merge until that is fixed\r\n\r\nThe thing is that, I don't know if it is even fixable.\r\n\r\nThis was a secondary method of handling the issue mentioned (the other method is also mentioned) and this is the less efficient (runtime wise) approach, as `[[no_unique_address]]` is just a suggestion to the compiler and not an obligation. The compiler is allowed to ignore this attribute. The much more scarier thing is that: MSVC exists.\r\n\r\nThe reason I opened this pull request is to show this as a more simpler alternative to the other more efficient (and more compiler-proof) but more complex method.\r\n\r\nThere is also a third method that I don't like but is an option, is that copy-pasting the AHashMap into HashSet and removing the value from code. This while enbetters the HashSet efficiency wise, this is code redundacy and may lead to seperation of the code again after some time. If this is an option that the maintainers are willing to look into, please let me know.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5330519090/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5330548473","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122544#issuecomment-5330548473","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122544","id":5330548473,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPbm2-Q","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T15:41:22Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T15:41:22Z","body":"IMO any performance regression here should be a blocker, this is a very critical type across the engine, and the better choice would naturally be the more efficient and compiler-proof option\r\n\r\nNot sure what the point of these changes are in that sense","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5330548473/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5331053733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122544#issuecomment-5331053733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122544","id":5331053733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPcFspQ","user":{"login":"Brogolem35","id":29329606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzI5NjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29329606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35","html_url":"https://github.com/Brogolem35","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T16:22:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T16:22:26Z","body":"> IMO any performance regression here should be a blocker, this is a very critical type across the engine, and the better choice would naturally be the more efficient and compiler-proof option\r\n\r\nWhen looked at the micro-benches, it is mostly improvement, but the practical ones show some minor regressions and I wasn't sure at what point they would be considered blocker so I opened it as discussion. Should have opened it as a draft from the beginning.\r\n\r\n> Not sure what the point of these changes are in that sense\r\n\r\nBecause the #112641 is up in the air for 9 months and the main critism it was receiving was its complexity. While [discussing this topic with another maintainer](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112641#pullrequestreview-3524167649) he suggested the use of `[[no_unique_address]]` and I knew it even before that but was hesitant to use it because C++ being C++. This is a proof of concept of that convo. This is much less complex but practically less efficient.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5331053733/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]